      "id": 1,
      "text": "Rotherhithe’s name comes from the Anglo‑Saxon word “Redriff”, meaning a cattle‑landing haven, first noted by Samuel Pepys.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
