      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Brunel Museum on the Thames Path celebrates Isambard Kingdom Brunel, who built the famous Thames Tunnel through Rotherhithe.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townandvillageguide.com/Greater_London/Rotherhithe.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The old Rotherhithe Town Hall now houses a library and museum, preserving the area’s maritime heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rotherhithe",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Rotherhithe once hosted a Norwegian, Finnish and Swedish church, reflecting its historic seafarers’ mission roots.",
